                  "no": 22,
                  "professor": "Professor Green – Sustainability",
                  "prompt": "Today we will discuss what consumers should prioritize when buying products. Some argue that choosing durable, repairable items reduces waste and benefits the environment over time. Others believe that supporting companies developing green technologies, such as energy-efficient devices or low-impact materials, drives broader industry change. What do you think consumers should prioritize?",
                  "posts": [
                    {
                      "name": "John",
                      "text": "I think consumers should prioritize durability. A product that lasts for years and can be repaired keeps us from constantly buying replacements and throwing old ones away, which directly reduces waste and production energy. When we clearly prefer durable goods, companies are also motivated to design sturdier, easier-to-fix items. To me, long-term use is one of the most practical ways to protect the environment."
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "Amy",
                      "text": "I believe consumers should support companies that invest in environmentally friendly technologies. Even a durable product may be manufactured using excessive energy or polluting processes. When we choose companies committed to cleaner materials and energy-efficient designs, we encourage industry-wide change in how products are made. That is why I think directing our money toward green innovation has a greater long-term impact than durability alone."
                    }
                  ],
                  "minWords": 100
